 "pforecast": null,
 "name": "Oceanum New Zealand 5km ERA5 wave hindcast parameters",
 "description": "This dataset contains gridded wave parameters produced by Oceanum using the SWAN wave model at 5km resolution over New Zealand waters. The dataset spans 1993 to 2026 at hourly resolution. 38 gridded parameters including full spectrum and partitions are provided over the full computational domain covering New Zealand waters and adjacent Pacific and Southern Ocean regions (165-180\u00b0E, 48-34\u00b0S). The model captures wave generation, propagation, and transformation processes around New Zealand's complex coastline, including the interaction between Southern Ocean swell and locally generated wind waves, and includes wave-current interactions through coupling with tidal and ocean reanalysis currents. Forcing is provided by ERA5 reanalysis winds from the European Centre for Medium-Range Weather Forecasts, with ocean currents combining NZ tidal constituents and Copernicus CMEMS ocean reanalysis surface currents. Spectral boundary conditions are supplied by Oceanum's global WW3 ERA5 wave model. Bathymetry is prescribed from the General Bathymetric Charts of the Oceans (GEBCO 2025). This gridded dataset is suitable for applications including coastal engineering design, metocean assessments, nearshore wave climate characterisation, offshore renewable energy resource evaluation, and climate impact studies around New Zealand. Corresponding wave spectra at selected sites are available in oceanum_wave_nzpar_era5_spec.",
